.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH "bead update" 1  "bead update " 
.SH NAME
bead update \- Update an issue
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbead update\fR [\fB\-\-status\fR] [\fB\-\-assignee\fR] [\fB\-\-clear\-assignee\fR] [\fB\-\-notes\fR] [\fB\-\-append\-notes\fR] [\fB\-\-notes\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-if\-revision\fR] [\fB\-\-fencing\-token\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-title\fR] [\fB\-\-description\fR] [\fB\-\-description\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-clear\-description\fR] [\fB\-\-priority\fR] [\fB\-\-reason\fR] [\fB\-\-issue\-type\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIID\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Update issue fields atomically.
.PP
Updates one or more issue fields in a single atomic transaction.
All validations and mutations occur together; any failure leaves the
issue unchanged. Changing status to \*(Aqclosed\*(Aq requires the \*(Aqclose\*(Aq command
instead. Use \*(Aqreopen\*(Aq to transition from closed to open.
.PP
EXAMPLES:
  bead update ID \-\-status in_progress                # Start working on an issue
  bead update ID \-\-assignee alice                    # Assign to alice
  bead update ID \-\-notes "Investigated root cause"   # Add investigation notes
  bead update ID \-\-append\-notes "Second investigation pass"
  bead update ID \-\-notes\-file investigation.txt
  bead update ID \-\-title "Revised task" \-\-description\-file details.txt
  bead update ID \-\-priority 1 \-\-reason "Urgency reviewed"
  bead update ID \-\-issue\-type investigation \-\-clear\-description
  cat investigation.txt | bead update ID \-\-notes\-file \-
  bead update ID \-\-clear\-assignee                    # Clear assignment (open only)
  bead update ID \-\-status in_progress \-\-if\-revision 3 # With revision guard
.PP
STATUS TRANSITIONS:
  Valid transitions depend on the current base status:
  \- open can transition to: in_progress, deferred
  \- in_progress can transition to: open, deferred, closed (via \*(Aqclose\*(Aq command)
  \- deferred can transition to: open, closed (via \*(Aqclose\*(Aq command)
  \- closed can only transition to: open (via \*(Aqreopen\*(Aq command)
.PP
EDITABLE FIELDS:
  Title, description, priority, issue type, notes, status and assignment.
  \-\-description, \-\-description\-file and \-\-clear\-description are exclusive.
  Empty description or notes values clear the corresponding text.
  \-\-priority requires a nonblank \-\-reason and records the actor and old/new
  priorities. An unchanged priority emits no priority event.
  Scalar metadata edits on closed issues preserve their close record.
  Use \*(Aqbead label add|remove\*(Aq and \*(Aqbead dep add|remove\*(Aq for related records.
.PP
ASSIGNMENT:
  \-\-assignee and \-\-clear\-assignee are mutually exclusive.
  \-\-clear\-assignee only works for open assigned issues.
  For in_progress issues, use \*(Aqbead release\*(Aq to return to open/unassigned.
.PP
BLOCKED STATUS:
  Setting \-\-status blocked sets manual_blocked=true and retains base status.
  Setting \-\-status open clears manual blocking and sets base status to open.
  Closed issues cannot use \-\-status open (use \*(Aqreopen\*(Aq instead).
.PP
REVISION GUARDS:
  \-\-if\-revision N provides optimistic concurrency control.
  If the issue\*(Aqs current revision doesn\*(Aqt match N, the update fails with
  exit code 4 and a conflict message. This prevents silent lost updates
  when multiple agents or humans modify the same issue concurrently.
.PP
All updates are atomic. Invalid transitions or conflicts exit with code 4
without changing any fields or timestamps.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-status\fR \fI<STATUS>\fR
New status
.TP
\fB\-\-assignee\fR \fI<ASSIGNEE>\fR
New assignee
.TP
\fB\-\-clear\-assignee\fR
Clear assignee (only for open assigned issues)
.TP
\fB\-\-notes\fR \fI<NOTES>\fR
New notes
.TP
\fB\-\-append\-notes\fR \fI<APPEND_NOTES>\fR
Append notes atomically to the existing notes field
.TP
\fB\-\-notes\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read notes from a UTF\-8 file, or stdin with \-
.TP
\fB\-\-if\-revision\fR \fI<IF_REVISION>\fR
Expected revision for optimistic concurrency control
.TP
\fB\-\-fencing\-token\fR \fI<FENCING_TOKEN>\fR
Fencing token for lease validation (advanced usage)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Dry run: show what would happen without making changes
.TP
\fB\-\-title\fR \fI<TITLE>\fR
Replace the title (1\-4096 UTF\-8 bytes)
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR
Replace the description; an empty value clears it
.TP
\fB\-\-description\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read the description from a UTF\-8 file, or stdin with \-
.TP
\fB\-\-clear\-description\fR
Clear the description to an empty string
.TP
\fB\-\-priority\fR \fI<PRIORITY>\fR
Set priority from 0 through 4, with an audit reason
.TP
\fB\-\-reason\fR \fI<REASON>\fR
Nonblank explanation for the supplied priority
.TP
\fB\-\-issue\-type\fR \fI<ISSUE_TYPE>\fR
Replace the issue type with a nonempty native type name
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
Issue ID
